      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lewiston was named after Benjamin Franklin Lewis, the adopted son of founder Tom Palmer who ran a gold mine on the Trinity River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lewiston%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Once a booming Gold Rush hub, Lewiston still carries the charm of the past with historic buildings and hidden treasures waiting to be discovered.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitlewistonca.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Trinity River cuts through Lewiston’s heart, flowing directly under the Old Lewiston Bridge that still stands today.",
